<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mengistu Haile Mariam</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1937">1937</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mengistu Haile Mariam was an Ethiopian army officer who rose to lead the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/derg">Derg</a>, the military council that overthrew Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haile-selassie">Haile Selassie</a> in 1974. The coup ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a> and the Solomonic monarchy. Mengistu ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> as a Marxist dictator until 1991.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mengistu-haile-mariam.jpg" alt="Mengistu Haile Mariam" width="300" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mengistu_Haile_Mariam_official_portrait,_1977-1978.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Meeting at the Fourth Division headquarters it elected Major <b>Mengistu Haile Mariam</b> chairman and Major Atnafu Abate vice-chairman.</blockquote><a href="/empire/derg">Derg · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Haile Selassie died in custody on 27 August 1975, most likely murdered on the orders of <b>Mengistu Haile Mariam</b>, ending a dynasty that had survived Adal invasion, the Zemene Mesafint, and Italian occupation across 704 years.</blockquote><a href="/empire/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Mengistu Haile Mariam</b> became president, and the Workers' Party of Ethiopia was proclaimed the leading force of state and society.</blockquote><a href="/state/peoples-democratic-republic-of-ethiopia">People's Democratic Republic of Ethiopia</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in the Galla-Sidamo Governorate. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p></section>
